<article class="env-lemma" id="0GF5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GF5">Lemma <span data-tag="0GF5">59.104.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Then the category fibred in groupoids </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  p : \mathcal{S} \longrightarrow (\mathit{Sch}/S)_ h  \]
</div>
  <p> whose fibre category over $U$ is the category $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (U_{\acute{e}tale})$ of sheaves on the small étale site of $U$ is a stack in groupoids. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      To prove the lemma we will check conditions (1), (2), and (3) of More on Flatness, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EX9" data-tag="0EX9">38.37.13</a>. 
    <p>
      Condition (1) holds because we have glueing for sheaves (and Zariski coverings are étale coverings). See Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/04TR" data-tag="04TR">7.26.4</a>. 
    <p>
      To see condition (2), suppose that $f : X \to Y$ is a surjective, flat, proper morphism of finite presentation over $S$ with $Y$ affine. Then we have descent for $\{ X \to Y\} $ by either Lemma <a href="/tag/0GF2" data-tag="0GF2">59.104.5</a> or Lemma <a href="/tag/0GF0" data-tag="0GF0">59.104.3</a>. 
    <p>
      Condition (3) follows immediately from the more general Lemma <a href="/tag/0GF4" data-tag="0GF4">59.104.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>